    <briefdescription>
<para><ref refid="classdap_1_1_reader" kindref="compound">Reader</ref> thread that parses DAP messages from stdin and passes each one to onMessage. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Runs one background JUCE thread. The thread reads Content-Length framed messages: it reads the header block, then the body, and parses the body as JSON. A body that does not parse is skipped. The thread ends when stdin fails or reaches its end, or when stop is signalled.</para>
<para>onMessage runs on the reader thread. <ref refid="class_whatdbg" kindref="compound">Whatdbg</ref> sets it to call <ref refid="class_processor_1aec3293e8c29b96cb2527f487286ad0b4" kindref="member">Processor::addRequest</ref>.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para><ref refid="classdap_1_1_reader_1a9e3d24e83e5c326d7d53f577b9efc5b5" kindref="member">~Reader()</ref> is the sole caller of <ref refid="classdap_1_1_reader_1a4ef3503bdf9aaa16b363e6261e60fc1a" kindref="member">stop()</ref>. It joins the background thread on destruction. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
